    fields:  # 8268
      statement: "Every change that can break a test is exercised by the per-PR gate. VIOLATED: smart-test's first check is 'did any Python source file change?', scoped to packages/*/src. A change confined to .agent/hooks/, scripts/ or tests/ makes it print 'No Python source files changed - skipping tests' and run NOTHING. Demonstrated 2026-07-29 on the transcript-scrubber branch: smart-test ran zero tests while the tree contained a genuinely red test (test_watcher_lifecycle::test_orphan_sweep_archives_dead_session_files). The red test was found only by an adversarial review; the gate would have let it reach dev, where it would surface in the twice-daily full-suite run. This is worse for governance paths than ordinary ones, because .agent/hooks/** and scripts/{auto-pr,install-hooks,...} are exactly the files AGENTS.md marks as requiring extra care."  # 8268
      root_cause: "scripts/smart-test gates on a changed-file predicate limited to packages/*/src before it ever consults the test map. Separately, .agent/hooks/_shared/top_level_test_map.py maps <name>.py -> tests/test_<name>.py with no hyphen normalisation (its docstring assumes those filenames are snake_case), so a kebab-case hook module maps to nothing even when the gate does run; and .sh files under _shared/ are excluded outright by an .endswith('.py') guard, so no shell hook change can ever select a test."  # 8268
